    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0461" n="357" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg357"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.13/7.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 7, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>You will immediately inform the Cuban Government that the amnesty bill seems to
                    be not only an injustice to the American citizens <pb facs="0462" n="358"
                        xml:id="pg358"/> affected but also to effect such a withdrawal of due
                    protection to property and individual liberty of Cuba as to excite this
                    Government’s concern. In view of its rights and obligations under the Treaty of
                    Relations of 1903, the Government of the United States expresses its firm
                    conviction that upon final study of this harmful measure the President of Cuba
                    will not permit it to become a law.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
